{"pulasti": [{"id": "pulasti", "headword": "पुलस्ति", "headword_slp1": "pulasti", "fold": "pulasti", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Pulasti or Pulastin in the yajurveda Saṃhitās denotes ‘wearing the hair plain,’ as opposed to kapardin, ‘wearing the hair in braids.’\nFoot notes taittirīya Saṃhitā, iv. 5, 9, 1; Vājasaneyi Saṃhitā, xvi. 43.\nkāṭhaka Saṃhītā, xvii. 15. Cf. Zimmer, Altindisches Leben, 265.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["pulasti", "పులస్తి", "ಪುಲಸ್ತಿ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["pulasti", "పులస్తి", "ಪುಲಸ್ತಿ"]}], "pulinda": [{"id": "pulinda", "headword": "पुलिन्द", "headword_slp1": "pulinda", "fold": "pulinda", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Pulinda is the name of an outcast tribe mentioned with the Andhras in the aitareya brāhmaṇa, but not in the śāṅkhāyana śrauta sūtra, in connexion with the story of śunaḥśepa. The Pulindas again appear associated with the Andhras in the time of Aśoka.\nFoot notes vii. 18.\nxv. 26.\nVincent Smith, Zeitschrift der Deutschen Morgenländischen Gesellschaft, 56, 652.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["pulinda", "పులిన్ద", "ಪುಲಿನ್ದ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["pulinda", "పులిన్ద", "ಪುಲಿನ್ದ"]}], "pulikaya": [{"id": "pulIkaya", "headword": "पुलीकय", "headword_slp1": "pulIkaya", "fold": "pulikaya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Pulīkaya. See purīkaya.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["puleekaya", "puliikaya", "pulīkaya", "పులీకయ", "ಪುಲೀಕಯ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["puleekaya", "puliikaya", "pulīkaya", "పులీకయ", "ಪುಲೀಕಯ"]}], "pulika": [{"id": "pulIkA", "headword": "पुलीका", "headword_slp1": "pulIkA", "fold": "pulika", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Pulīkā seems to designate some kind of bird in the Maitrāyaṇī Saṃhitā (iii. 14, 5). The name appears in the form of kulīkā in the Vājasaneyi Saṃhitā (xxiv. 24).", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["puleekaa", "puliikaa", "pulīkā", "పులీకా", "ಪುಲೀಕಾ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["puleekaa", "puliikaa", "pulīkā", "పులీకా", "ಪುಲೀಕಾ"]}], "pulusa pracina-yogya": [{"id": "puluza prAcIna-yogya", "headword": "पुलुष प्राचीन-योग्य", "headword_slp1": "puluza prAcIna-yogya", "fold": "pulusa pracina-yogya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Puluṣa prācīna-yogya (‘descendant of Prācīnayoga’) is the name of a teacher, a pupil of dṛti Aindroti śaunaka, in a vaṃśa (list of teachers) of the Jaiminīya upaniṣad brāhmaṇa (iii. 40, 2). He taught pauluṣi satyayajña.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["puluSha praacheena", "puluSha praacheena-yogya", "puluSha praacheenayogya", "puluSha praachiina", "puluSha praachiina-yogya", "puluSha praachiinayogya", "puluṣa prācīna", "puluṣa prācīna-yogya", "puluṣa prācīnayogya", "yogya", "पुलुष प्राचीन", "पुलुष प्राचीनयोग्य", "योग्य", "పులుష ప్రాచీన", "పులుష ప్రాచీన-యోగ్య", "పులుష ప్రాచీనయోగ్య", "యోగ్య", "ಪುಲುಷ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ", "ಪುಲುಷ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ-ಯೋಗ್ಯ", "ಪುಲುಷ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನಯೋಗ್ಯ", "ಯೋಗ್ಯ"], "synonyms_slp1": ["puluSha praacheena", "puluSha praacheena-yogya", "puluSha praacheenayogya", "puluSha praachiina", "puluSha praachiina-yogya", "puluSha praachiinayogya", "puluṣa prācīna", "puluṣa prācīna-yogya", "puluṣa prācīnayogya", "yogya", "puluza prAcIna", "puluza prAcInayogya", "yogya", "పులుష ప్రాచీన", "పులుష ప్రాచీన-యోగ్య", "పులుష ప్రాచీనయోగ్య", "యోగ్య", "ಪುಲುಷ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ", "ಪುಲುಷ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನ-ಯೋಗ್ಯ", "ಪುಲುಷ ಪ್ರಾಚೀನಯೋಗ್ಯ", "ಯೋಗ್ಯ"]}], "pulya": [{"id": "pUlya", "headword": "पूल्य", "headword_slp1": "pUlya", "fold": "pulya", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "vedic-index-macdonell-keith", "senses": [{"gloss": "Pūlya, or pūlpa, in the Atharvaveda seems to mean ‘shrivelled grain’ (cf. Lājā).\nFoot notes xiv. 2, 63. Cf. Whitney, Translation of the Atharvaveda, 765.", "gloss_language": "en"}], "synonyms": ["poolpa", "poolya", "puulpa", "puulya", "pūlpa", "pūlya", "पू